00:04:53.400 --> 00:04:58.780
The catalyst is the Clarity Act introduction that seeks comprehensive federal crypto rules.

00:04:59.240 --> 00:05:05.200
The technical setup waits for a volume spike above the 20-day average after any regulatory headline.

00:05:05.840 --> 00:05:11.020
Risk assessment notes that regulatory delays or negative amendments could pressure prices,

00:05:11.580 --> 00:05:17.460
so no position is taken yet. Confidence sits at low because this remains a single factor regulatory

00:05:17.460 --> 00:05:23.660
headline without volume or price confirmation. The setup demonstrates how to wait for both a

00:05:23.660 --> 00:05:29.980
policy catalyst and confirming volume before entering volatile assets, avoiding the trap of reacting

00:05:29.980 --> 00:05:36.240
to headlines alone. Listeners learn the value of predefined trigger criteria rather than chasing

00:05:36.240 --> 00:05:41.900
every regulatory rumor. The Clarity Act would establish a federal framework that could reduce

00:05:41.900 --> 00:05:48.120
enforcement uncertainty for exchanges and custodians, yet the bill remains in early stages with no

00:05:48.120 --> 00:05:54.660
timeline for passage. I am specifically watching for any Senate markup announcement or co-sponsor count

00:05:54.660 --> 00:06:01.060
above 20 before considering entry. The trigger that would activate a position is a same-day volume

00:06:01.060 --> 00:06:06.440
reading above the 20-day average paired with a positive close above the prior week's high.

