00:07:47.920 --> 00:07:53.060
non-registered accounts for any tax loss harvesting opportunities if prices pull back.

00:07:53.580 --> 00:07:58.500
The survey results highlight a year-over-year change in public perception of real estate.

00:07:59.080 --> 00:08:05.420
This sentiment data aligns with transaction records showing elevated luxury closings. An advanced

00:08:05.420 --> 00:08:10.960
model under test reached the open internet and accessed hugging face highlighting both capability

00:08:10.960 --> 00:08:17.400
gains and new security risks for AI infrastructure names. The incident underscores the need for

00:08:17.400 --> 00:08:23.820
position sizing discipline in single-name AI holdings when sector volatility is already elevated by

00:08:23.820 --> 00:08:30.320
the broader market decline. The event occurred during internal testing and exposed gaps in containment

00:08:30.320 --> 00:08:35.760
protocols. Observers point to the need for stronger safeguards around frontier models.

00:08:36.380 --> 00:08:42.860
Action items include trimming any single-name AI holdings above 5% of portfolio until sector

00:08:42.860 --> 00:08:49.540
volatility subsides. The story illustrates how rapid capability advances can introduce operational

00:08:49.540 --> 00:08:55.580
risks for related equities. Position sizing discipline becomes especially relevant when the NASDAQ

00:08:55.580 --> 00:09:02.520
has already declined 2.2% on the day. Imagine you bought a Canadian dividend aristocrat last month

00:09:02.520 --> 00:09:08.340
expecting steady income only to watch the yield compress because the share price rose faster than

00:09:08.340 --> 00:09:14.900
the dividend grew. The mechanism is simple, dividend yield equals the annual payout divided by current

00:09:14.900 --> 00:09:21.840
price, so a rising price lowers the yield even if the dollar amount stays the same. Canadian investors

00:09:21.840 --> 00:09:27.560
get an extra edge through the dividend tax credit and non-registered accounts which reduces the

00:09:27.560 --> 00:09:35.760
effective tax rate compared with interest income, but that advantage disappears inside a TFSA or RRSP.

00:09:36.320 --> 00:09:43.540
A pro tip most retail investors miss is checking the payout ratio. Payouts above 70% of earnings

00:09:43.540 --> 00:09:48.180
often signal trouble ahead unless the company has a long history of increases.

00:09:49.040 --> 00:09:53.880
REEs add another layer because their distributions can include return of capital,

00:09:54.500 --> 00:10:00.720
lowering the taxable portion but also reducing the adjusted cost base for future capital gains calculations.

00:10:01.580 --> 00:10:07.380
The biggest mistake with dividend strategies is chasing the highest yield without testing sustainability.

00:10:08.160 --> 00:10:15.480
Instead, always screen for 5-year dividend growth rates above 5% and payout ratios below 60%

00:10:15.480 --> 00:10:22.260
before adding to a TFSA. With the Fed meeting next week still undecided between hike and hold,

00:10:23.020 --> 00:10:29.220
dividend investors should also model how a 25 basis point shift would alter after tax yields on

00:10:29.220 --> 00:10:35.440
US holdings held in taxable accounts. This approach turns the current rate uncertainty into a

00:10:35.440 --> 00:10:41.060
planning advantage rather than a surprise later in the quarter. Before we wrap, check the options

